Feature Added
Pause/Resume Animation System + Moon Translation Effect
Description
This contribution improves the OpenGL graphics project by introducing control over animation playback and adding dynamic movement to the moon.
Users can now pause and resume all animations in real time, and the moon has been enhanced with smooth translation movement across the sky.
Implemented Features
Pause all animations (freeze system state)
Resume animations (continue motion smoothly)
Continuous moon translation in both X and Y directions
Smooth orbital-like moon drifting motion
Integration with existing day/night system
Preserved animation consistency after resume
Controls
Press P → Pause all animations
Press C → Resume animations
Press X → Toggle Day/Night mode
Mouse movement → Interactive celestial scaling
Left click → Interaction with celestial objects
Technical Details
The feature is implemented using time-based animation control and transformation techniques:
isAnimated flag → Master switch for all animations
Conditional update loop inside update() function
sin() and cos() functions → Smooth moon trajectory movement
glTranslatef() → Applied moon displacement transformations
State preservation → Ensures seamless resume after pause
Frame-based animation control using waveTime
Functions Added / Modified
update() (enhanced with pause/resume logic)
Moon translation logic (moonTranslateX, moonTranslateY)
Integrated animation control system
Additional Enhancements
Smooth moon drifting path across sky
Stable animation freeze without graphical glitches
Seamless transition between paused and running states
Improved user control over animation flow
